itbdev/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kitbdev/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"This should be done in `gdscript_editor` `complete_code` when it gets the completion options instead.\r\n- like in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/96375\r\n\r\nIt is a gdscript specific problem, and it also happens with external editors connected via LSP, so CodeEdit should not need to be changed. CodeEdit also tries to avoid language details, it doesn't know what parenthesis are for, and it uses things like `brace_completion_pair` to avoid hardcoding \"(\".","state":"CHANGES_REQUESTED","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105528#pullrequestreview-2794367076","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105528","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","_links":{"html":{"href":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/105528#pullrequestreview-2794367076"},"pull_request":{"href":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/105528"}},"submitted_at":"2025-04-25T14:40:01Z","commit_id":null},{"id":2795822303,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc6mpNzf","user":{"login":"tehKaiN","id":16180344,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2MTgwMzQ0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16180344?u=4b576ae2fa5ba4b3a52dab8eee4b930f8f3bab19&v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN","html_url":"https://github.com/tehKaiN","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/tehKaiN/follo